Content
-------

This distribution includes four solvers

  bin/yices       (for the Yices 2 language)
  bin/yices-smt   (for SMT-LIB 1.2)
  bin/yices-smt2  (for SMT-LIB 2.0)
  bin/yices-sat   (sat solver, DIMACS format)

and the Yices libraries and header files

  lib/__DYLIB__
  lib/libyices.a
  lib/pkgconfig/yices.pc
  include/yices.h
  include/yices_types.h
  include/yices_limits.h
  include/yices_exit_codes.h


Examples and documentation are in the examples and doc directories.


The Yices shared library and the binaries other than the sat solver require
GMP version __GMP__ or compatible. GMP is copyright Free Software Foundation
(see NOTICES).

GMP must be installed as a dynamic library in /usr/local/lib for
Yices to find it.



Installation
------------

The library's install name is '@rpath/__DYLIB__'. A program that links against
it must supply a run-path, normally with
`-Wl,-rpath,/path/to/yices/lib` at link time, or set `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` at
run time.
This distribution includes a shell script to copy the files into an
installation prefix. For a non-destructive installation, choose a fresh
prefix that you own:

   YICES_PREFIX="$HOME/.local/yices-2.8.0"
   ./install-yices "$YICES_PREFIX"

The installer does not copy `lib/libyices.a` or `doc/manual.pdf`. Keep the
extracted distribution when you need the static archive or the manual.

The installer refuses to replace existing Yices files or links. To
intentionally replace an installation in a shared prefix after reviewing it:

   sudo ./install-yices --replace-existing /usr/local

Try ./install-yices --help for more explanations.


For more information, please visit https://yices.csl.sri.com.
